Figure 1a presents a schematic overview of the on-chip PNN accelerator, wherein compressed and flattened input features from the dataset are encoded onto coherent optical amplitudes at a single wavelength (λ). Within the topology-optimized scattering region, the encoded optical fields undergo complex interference and scattering interactions throughout the device volume. The scattering region itself is designed to support non-uniform optical transport21,28, with routing behavior that adapts to the spatial distribution of optical inputs, efficiently redistributing optical power from the \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
