To experimentally demonstrate the feasibility of our designs, we fabricate PNN accelerators for MNIST and MedNIST datasets on the SOI platform (see Methods). Figures 5a and b show the scanning electron microscope (SEM) images of the fabricated 20 × 20 µm2 MNIST and 30 × 20 µm2 MedNIST PNN accelerators, respectively, highlighting their compact footprints. Both input and output waveguides are designed to support the fundamental transverse-electric (TE) mode at 1550 nm, with a width of 500 nm and height of 220 nm. The minimal feature size across the device is 80 nm.Fig. 5PNN accelerators fabricated on the SOI platform.
